[[:db/retract 17592186152477 :question/answer-fields 17592186149420] [:db/retract 17592186152477 :question/answer-fields 17592186149414] [:db/retract 17592186152477 :question/answer-fields 17592186149423] [:db/retract 17592186152478 :question/answer-fields 17592186149432] [:db/retract 17592186152478 :question/answer-fields 17592186149426] {:db/id 17592186152094 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c4019e4a-38d9-5f9b-be44-5c0d23af5290" "question-0ff193af-a6fe-56c6-94b7-27cf32c1ffe5" "question-d23e3ed0-5575-5880-b9bf-7ff1adfe9936" "question-c54d6f9f-c7e1-5ec9-825f-3e37025371fc" "question-e3dce9be-488e-597e-98f1-e5e643b35fa5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151843 :question/problem "Given that $4a \\equiv 4b \\,(\\textrm{mod}\\,8),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n- $a \\equiv b \\quad(\\textrm{mod}\\,4)$\n\n- $a \\equiv b \\quad(\\textrm{mod}\\,2)$\n\n- $a \\equiv b \\quad(\\textrm{mod}\\,8)$" :question/worked-solution "The division property of modular arithmetic states that for $k\\neq 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka\\equiv kb\\quad(\\textrm{mod} \\,kn) \\qquad \\Longleftrightarrow\\qquad a \\equiv b \\quad(\\textrm{mod}\\, n).\n$$\n\nWe're asked to consider the following statement:\n\n$$\n4a \\equiv 4b \\quad(\\textrm{mod}\\,8)\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\text{gcd}(4,8) =4.$\n\nApplying the division property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a & ≡4b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\ 4\\cdot a & ≡4\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4\\cdot 2) \\\\ \\cancel{4}\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{4}\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{4}\\cdot 2) \\\\ a & ≡b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152095 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-eaf9f361-8af6-5a67-abf5-86a0bbac7a1d" "question-cdd37720-ffc4-552d-8b81-f3aa2f866efb" "question-0db74dcd-d670-5d6c-b7fa-69c8b873b4a0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151842 :question/problem "If $ka \\equiv kb \\: (\\textrm{mod} \\,7)$\nis equivalent to $%\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\na \\equiv b \\:(\\textrm{mod} \\,7),$\nwhich of the following could be the value of $k?$\n\n- $k=-12$\n\n- $k=4$\n\n- $k=-14$" :question/worked-solution "The division property of modular arithmetic states that\n\n$$\nka\\equiv kb\\quad(\\textrm{mod} \\,n) \\qquad \\Longleftrightarrow\\qquad a \\equiv b \\quad(\\textrm{mod}\\, n)\n$$\n\nprovided that $k$ and $n$ are coprime. In other words, we require $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1.$\n\nIn this case, the modulus $n=7.$ Let's consider each value of $k$ in turn.\n\n- If $k=-12,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n) = \\text{gcd}(-12,7) = 1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is valid for $k=-12.$\n\n- If $k=4,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n) = \\text{gcd}(4,7) = 1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is valid for $k=4.$\n\n- If $k=-14,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n) = \\text{gcd}(-14,7) = 7\\neq 1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is *not* valid for $k=-14.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152096 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ca808cf3-f807-5d95-a81f-b5460b52df5b" "question-00e9a03d-cb25-5bd2-bcfe-67d16e1b93d4" "question-3f8540b5-4c77-553b-a7f5-1fd3c7ffd53b" "question-73a43b1a-0275-523e-ad37-d72b83b2b870" "question-a253797f-7a56-5114-8318-23c6ded7e919"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151858 :question/problem "Given that $15a \\equiv 15b \\,(\\textrm{mod}\\,20),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n- $a \\equiv b \\quad (\\textrm{mod}\\, 20)$\n\n- $a \\equiv b \\quad (\\textrm{mod}\\,4)$\n\n- $7a \\equiv 7b \\quad (\\textrm{mod}\\,4)$" :question/worked-solution "The division properties of modular arithmetic state the following:\n\n- For $k\\neq 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka \\equiv kb \\quad(\\text{mod}\\,kn) \\qquad \\Longleftrightarrow \\qquad a \\equiv b \\quad(\\textrm{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\n- For $\\text{gcd}(k, n) = 1,$ we have \n\n$$\nka \\equiv kb \\quad(\\text{mod}\\,n) \\qquad \\Longleftrightarrow \\qquad a \\equiv b \\quad(\\textrm{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Applying the first property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15a & ≡15b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,20) \\\\ 5\\cdot 3\\cdot a & ≡5\\cdot 3\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5\\cdot 4) \\\\ \\cancel{5}\\cdot 3\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{5}\\cdot 3\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{5}\\cdot 4) \\\\ 3a & ≡3b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\gcd(3,4)=1,$ by the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n3a \\equiv 3b \\quad(\\textrm{mod}\\,4) \\qquad \\Longleftrightarrow \\qquad a \\equiv b \\quad(\\textrm{mod}\\,4)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. By statement II and the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)\\,⟺\\,7a≡7b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-c4019e4a-38d9-5f9b-be44-5c0d23af5290" :question/id #uuid "c4019e4a-38d9-5f9b-be44-5c0d23af5290" :question/math-academy-id "q-103171" :question/problem "Given that $2a≡2b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$" :question/worked-solution "The division property of modular arithmetic states that for $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWe're asked to consider the following statement:\n\n$$\n2a≡2b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\text{gcd}(2,8)=2.$\n\nApplying the division property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a & ≡2b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\ 2\\cdot a & ≡2\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2\\cdot 4) \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{2}\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{2}\\cdot 4) \\\\ a & ≡b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fc93f710-a95a-5049-bcda-b4e2876fa001"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fc93f710-a95a-5049-bcda-b4e2876fa001" :answer-field/id #uuid "fc93f710-a95a-5049-bcda-b4e2876fa001" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f51e8872-95d1-53a4-be14-a0d7848bcba9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-43a7e751-1cfd-5fee-b159-3b5f2b487bc3" "answer-9a6c4a6b-24ed-570f-8486-7fc8b14b4ff9" "answer-6e9f8253-0b3f-5665-a130-2f4bb45db984" "answer-f51e8872-95d1-53a4-be14-a0d7848bcba9" "answer-69bb5ea8-a037-5146-805c-1dd1ecec0c01"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43a7e751-1cfd-5fee-b159-3b5f2b487bc3" :answer/id #uuid "43a7e751-1cfd-5fee-b159-3b5f2b487bc3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a6c4a6b-24ed-570f-8486-7fc8b14b4ff9" :answer/id #uuid "9a6c4a6b-24ed-570f-8486-7fc8b14b4ff9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e9f8253-0b3f-5665-a130-2f4bb45db984" :answer/id #uuid "6e9f8253-0b3f-5665-a130-2f4bb45db984" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f51e8872-95d1-53a4-be14-a0d7848bcba9" :answer/id #uuid "f51e8872-95d1-53a4-be14-a0d7848bcba9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69bb5ea8-a037-5146-805c-1dd1ecec0c01" :answer/id #uuid "69bb5ea8-a037-5146-805c-1dd1ecec0c01" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0ff193af-a6fe-56c6-94b7-27cf32c1ffe5" :question/id #uuid "0ff193af-a6fe-56c6-94b7-27cf32c1ffe5" :question/math-academy-id "q-103191" :question/problem "Given that $6a≡6b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n- $2a≡2b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$\n- $3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)$" :question/worked-solution "The division property of modular arithmetic states that for $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWe're asked to consider the following statement:\n\n$$\n6a≡6b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\text{gcd}(6,9)=3.$\n\nApplying the division property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a & ≡6b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,9) \\\\ 3\\cdot 2\\cdot a & ≡3\\cdot 2\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,3\\cdot 3) \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot 2\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{3}\\cdot 2\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{3}\\cdot 3) \\\\ 2a & ≡2b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ac14ead2-1a03-5fa3-95d0-5a72490e2583"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ac14ead2-1a03-5fa3-95d0-5a72490e2583" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac14ead2-1a03-5fa3-95d0-5a72490e2583" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b5c3b253-f21f-58e1-98dc-54b06420dd03" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dd07f6b5-d64e-5f75-85b5-a565d52ddc05" "answer-b5c3b253-f21f-58e1-98dc-54b06420dd03" "answer-6333918e-5906-5548-8e59-11cfdafb53e4" "answer-2b40d7ae-81fd-5560-a3b6-1912b4d03c01" "answer-ffd323a5-6eca-50fb-aef2-a5207b006ddf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd07f6b5-d64e-5f75-85b5-a565d52ddc05" :answer/id #uuid "dd07f6b5-d64e-5f75-85b5-a565d52ddc05" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5c3b253-f21f-58e1-98dc-54b06420dd03" :answer/id #uuid "b5c3b253-f21f-58e1-98dc-54b06420dd03" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6333918e-5906-5548-8e59-11cfdafb53e4" :answer/id #uuid "6333918e-5906-5548-8e59-11cfdafb53e4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b40d7ae-81fd-5560-a3b6-1912b4d03c01" :answer/id #uuid "2b40d7ae-81fd-5560-a3b6-1912b4d03c01" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ffd323a5-6eca-50fb-aef2-a5207b006ddf" :answer/id #uuid "ffd323a5-6eca-50fb-aef2-a5207b006ddf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d23e3ed0-5575-5880-b9bf-7ff1adfe9936" :question/id #uuid "d23e3ed0-5575-5880-b9bf-7ff1adfe9936" :question/math-academy-id "q-103168" :question/problem "Given that $3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,12),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$" :question/worked-solution "The division property of modular arithmetic states that for $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWe're asked to consider the following statement:\n\n$$\n3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,12)\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\text{gcd}(3,12)=3.$\n\nApplying the division property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a & ≡3b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,12) \\\\ 3\\cdot a & ≡3\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,3\\cdot 4) \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{3}\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{3}\\cdot 4) \\\\ a & ≡b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5139e167-eff8-5fb2-95ba-ff706a30c921"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5139e167-eff8-5fb2-95ba-ff706a30c921" :answer-field/id #uuid "5139e167-eff8-5fb2-95ba-ff706a30c921" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e7f12825-c2b7-5186-8218-7c940c5283cf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9b4bf61e-6b83-5157-b763-8513937c1774" "answer-3ad3b1aa-93e7-5b73-a4b4-ec7fb6b5d2f8" "answer-e0a31f1f-fd54-58eb-b1f3-5e9c47ac9da1" "answer-e7f12825-c2b7-5186-8218-7c940c5283cf" "answer-be01c4c9-9b6c-5fb4-b2ec-7c85edac2cfd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b4bf61e-6b83-5157-b763-8513937c1774" :answer/id #uuid "9b4bf61e-6b83-5157-b763-8513937c1774" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ad3b1aa-93e7-5b73-a4b4-ec7fb6b5d2f8" :answer/id #uuid "3ad3b1aa-93e7-5b73-a4b4-ec7fb6b5d2f8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0a31f1f-fd54-58eb-b1f3-5e9c47ac9da1" :answer/id #uuid "e0a31f1f-fd54-58eb-b1f3-5e9c47ac9da1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7f12825-c2b7-5186-8218-7c940c5283cf" :answer/id #uuid "e7f12825-c2b7-5186-8218-7c940c5283cf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be01c4c9-9b6c-5fb4-b2ec-7c85edac2cfd" :answer/id #uuid "be01c4c9-9b6c-5fb4-b2ec-7c85edac2cfd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-eaf9f361-8af6-5a67-abf5-86a0bbac7a1d" :question/id #uuid "eaf9f361-8af6-5a67-abf5-86a0bbac7a1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-103018" :question/problem "If \n$ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10)$\nis equivalent to\n$a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10),$\nwhich of the following could be the value of $k?$\n\n- $k=12$\n- $k=3$\n- $k=-5$" :question/worked-solution "The division property of modular arithmetic states that\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\n$$\n\nprovided that $k$ and $n$ are coprime. In other words, we require $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1.$\n\nIn this case, the modulus $n=10.$ Let's consider each value of $k$ in turn.\n\n- If $k=12,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(12,10)=2\\ne 1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is *not* valid for $k=12.$\n\n- If $k=3,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(3,10)=1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is valid for $k=3.$\n\n- If $k=-5,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(-5,10)=5\\ne 1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is *not* valid for $k=-5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-68b518f5-1d9e-5140-a83d-d1e076453bbe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-68b518f5-1d9e-5140-a83d-d1e076453bbe" :answer-field/id #uuid "68b518f5-1d9e-5140-a83d-d1e076453bbe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a4b3e191-4f8f-5513-9308-e68abbfe8bcb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0d32cab0-a947-5df3-b52a-1e20d4a89706" "answer-19a4b986-70e3-5216-b16f-03a5fda6657d" "answer-636fa707-191d-5267-8fee-440385919afb" "answer-a4b3e191-4f8f-5513-9308-e68abbfe8bcb" "answer-5a04721a-ae8a-5b6e-8878-aabea63fdaaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d32cab0-a947-5df3-b52a-1e20d4a89706" :answer/id #uuid "0d32cab0-a947-5df3-b52a-1e20d4a89706" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19a4b986-70e3-5216-b16f-03a5fda6657d" :answer/id #uuid "19a4b986-70e3-5216-b16f-03a5fda6657d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-636fa707-191d-5267-8fee-440385919afb" :answer/id #uuid "636fa707-191d-5267-8fee-440385919afb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4b3e191-4f8f-5513-9308-e68abbfe8bcb" :answer/id #uuid "a4b3e191-4f8f-5513-9308-e68abbfe8bcb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a04721a-ae8a-5b6e-8878-aabea63fdaaa" :answer/id #uuid "5a04721a-ae8a-5b6e-8878-aabea63fdaaa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cdd37720-ffc4-552d-8b81-f3aa2f866efb" :question/id #uuid "cdd37720-ffc4-552d-8b81-f3aa2f866efb" :question/math-academy-id "q-103026" :question/problem "If \n$ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$\nis equivalent to\n$a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8),$\nwhich of the following could be the value of $k?$\n\n- $k=8$\n- $k=-12$\n- $k=-15$" :question/worked-solution "The division property of modular arithmetic states that\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\n$$\n\nprovided that $k$ and $n$ are coprime. In other words, we require $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1.$\n\nIn this case, the modulus $n=8.$ Let's consider each value of $k$ in turn.\n\n- If $k=8,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(8,8)=8\\ne 1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is *not* valid for $k=8.$\n\n- If $k=-12,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(-12,8)=4\\ne 1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is *not* valid for $k=-12.$\n\n- If $k=-15,$ then $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=\\text{gcd}(-15,8)=1.$ Therefore, our equivalence is valid for $k=-15.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-185bfed6-c6e9-5751-adee-92e27148dc54"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-185bfed6-c6e9-5751-adee-92e27148dc54" :answer-field/id #uuid "185bfed6-c6e9-5751-adee-92e27148dc54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a0f6d41d-dc0c-54e9-864e-febae8295631" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0ab1a91d-d33a-5e51-b220-e0e4da05d420" "answer-f95294ea-d39c-5f5e-8043-8a30f497210f" "answer-a3d03008-076d-5979-8ec2-d15997b802f9" "answer-ee51c39b-f541-5db9-9b1d-bc0125830007" "answer-a0f6d41d-dc0c-54e9-864e-febae8295631"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ab1a91d-d33a-5e51-b220-e0e4da05d420" :answer/id #uuid "0ab1a91d-d33a-5e51-b220-e0e4da05d420" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f95294ea-d39c-5f5e-8043-8a30f497210f" :answer/id #uuid "f95294ea-d39c-5f5e-8043-8a30f497210f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3d03008-076d-5979-8ec2-d15997b802f9" :answer/id #uuid "a3d03008-076d-5979-8ec2-d15997b802f9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee51c39b-f541-5db9-9b1d-bc0125830007" :answer/id #uuid "ee51c39b-f541-5db9-9b1d-bc0125830007" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0f6d41d-dc0c-54e9-864e-febae8295631" :answer/id #uuid "a0f6d41d-dc0c-54e9-864e-febae8295631" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ca808cf3-f807-5d95-a81f-b5460b52df5b" :question/id #uuid "ca808cf3-f807-5d95-a81f-b5460b52df5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-213392" :question/problem "Given that $3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)$\n- $4a≡4b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$" :question/worked-solution "The division properties of modular arithmetic state the following:\n\n- For $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\n- For $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1,$ we have \n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Applying the first property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a & ≡3b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,9) \\\\ 3\\cdot a & ≡3\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,3\\cdot 3) \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{3}\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{3}\\cdot 3) \\\\ a & ≡b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. By statement I and the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\\,⟺\\,4a≡4b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c26a95a5-c027-5bfd-8dc6-5ac33606e4cd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c26a95a5-c027-5bfd-8dc6-5ac33606e4cd" :answer-field/id #uuid "c26a95a5-c027-5bfd-8dc6-5ac33606e4cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dfb5e76a-e012-5b9d-add1-ff7fc168f39c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-81d02ebf-0e9e-55cb-a573-4ae072ffecb0" "answer-dfb5e76a-e012-5b9d-add1-ff7fc168f39c" "answer-411fcf4c-0dfe-5eb4-b277-2957160dccc5" "answer-ffca300c-7c35-5dd6-9629-dda4cf9c21da" "answer-74b71bad-1c7b-5ec7-82dd-47d6ce2c7ca6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81d02ebf-0e9e-55cb-a573-4ae072ffecb0" :answer/id #uuid "81d02ebf-0e9e-55cb-a573-4ae072ffecb0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfb5e76a-e012-5b9d-add1-ff7fc168f39c" :answer/id #uuid "dfb5e76a-e012-5b9d-add1-ff7fc168f39c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-411fcf4c-0dfe-5eb4-b277-2957160dccc5" :answer/id #uuid "411fcf4c-0dfe-5eb4-b277-2957160dccc5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ffca300c-7c35-5dd6-9629-dda4cf9c21da" :answer/id #uuid "ffca300c-7c35-5dd6-9629-dda4cf9c21da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74b71bad-1c7b-5ec7-82dd-47d6ce2c7ca6" :answer/id #uuid "74b71bad-1c7b-5ec7-82dd-47d6ce2c7ca6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-00e9a03d-cb25-5bd2-bcfe-67d16e1b93d4" :question/id #uuid "00e9a03d-cb25-5bd2-bcfe-67d16e1b93d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-213297" :question/problem "Given that $5a≡5b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,15),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$\n- $4a≡4b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,12)$" :question/worked-solution "The division properties of modular arithmetic state the following:\n\n- For $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\n- For $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1,$ we have \n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Applying the first property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a & ≡5b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\ 5\\cdot a & ≡5\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5\\cdot 3) \\\\ \\cancel{5}\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{5}\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{5}\\cdot 3) \\\\ a & ≡b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. By statement II and the first property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\\,⟺\\,4a≡4b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,12)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\n.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-27721e63-6adb-57d0-9211-64392779ba7d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-27721e63-6adb-57d0-9211-64392779ba7d" :answer-field/id #uuid "27721e63-6adb-57d0-9211-64392779ba7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-53ad8ef2-28c6-563f-b134-1a1539671090" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9a43e1b2-3043-5dfc-9827-55b5c21ef088" "answer-45974aae-697e-59ea-90f3-58a3d7ab07f5" "answer-53ad8ef2-28c6-563f-b134-1a1539671090" "answer-f17a369e-4ccb-56ba-89f8-03b525e4cd5c" "answer-8ef2cd18-60ec-5d72-8a48-14b406665bdf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a43e1b2-3043-5dfc-9827-55b5c21ef088" :answer/id #uuid "9a43e1b2-3043-5dfc-9827-55b5c21ef088" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45974aae-697e-59ea-90f3-58a3d7ab07f5" :answer/id #uuid "45974aae-697e-59ea-90f3-58a3d7ab07f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53ad8ef2-28c6-563f-b134-1a1539671090" :answer/id #uuid "53ad8ef2-28c6-563f-b134-1a1539671090" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f17a369e-4ccb-56ba-89f8-03b525e4cd5c" :answer/id #uuid "f17a369e-4ccb-56ba-89f8-03b525e4cd5c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ef2cd18-60ec-5d72-8a48-14b406665bdf" :answer/id #uuid "8ef2cd18-60ec-5d72-8a48-14b406665bdf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3f8540b5-4c77-553b-a7f5-1fd3c7ffd53b" :question/id #uuid "3f8540b5-4c77-553b-a7f5-1fd3c7ffd53b" :question/math-academy-id "q-77149" :question/problem "Given that $6a≡6b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$\n- $4a≡4b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,16)$" :question/worked-solution "The division properties of modular arithmetic state the following:\n\n- For $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\n- For $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1,$ we have \n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Applying the first property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a & ≡6b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\ 2\\cdot 3\\cdot a & ≡2\\cdot 3\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2\\cdot 4) \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{2}\\cdot 4) \\\\ 3a & ≡3b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $gcd(3,4)=1,$ by the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. By statement I and the first property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)\\,⟺\\,4a≡4b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,16)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c0b32a4d-27a1-5f09-9586-0eda4f6e258c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c0b32a4d-27a1-5f09-9586-0eda4f6e258c" :answer-field/id #uuid "c0b32a4d-27a1-5f09-9586-0eda4f6e258c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d7d8562b-f70b-5c3a-a72d-d5fb98ff423c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ebce1721-add9-5499-a872-ac033f683890" "answer-d7d8562b-f70b-5c3a-a72d-d5fb98ff423c" "answer-6d525025-b858-597d-81f2-ca5669d4e790" "answer-b21f5aff-6f4d-5471-a3b6-6cc217f29b8d" "answer-26bee83a-d0b0-540d-abf4-27c985c7467f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebce1721-add9-5499-a872-ac033f683890" :answer/id #uuid "ebce1721-add9-5499-a872-ac033f683890" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7d8562b-f70b-5c3a-a72d-d5fb98ff423c" :answer/id #uuid "d7d8562b-f70b-5c3a-a72d-d5fb98ff423c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d525025-b858-597d-81f2-ca5669d4e790" :answer/id #uuid "6d525025-b858-597d-81f2-ca5669d4e790" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b21f5aff-6f4d-5471-a3b6-6cc217f29b8d" :answer/id #uuid "b21f5aff-6f4d-5471-a3b6-6cc217f29b8d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26bee83a-d0b0-540d-abf4-27c985c7467f" :answer/id #uuid "26bee83a-d0b0-540d-abf4-27c985c7467f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-73a43b1a-0275-523e-ad37-d72b83b2b870" :question/id #uuid "73a43b1a-0275-523e-ad37-d72b83b2b870" :question/math-academy-id "q-213296" :question/problem "Given that $10a≡10b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$\n- $5a≡5b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,15)$" :question/worked-solution "The division properties of modular arithmetic state the following:\n\n- For $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\n- For $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1,$ we have \n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Applying the first property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10a & ≡10b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\ 2\\cdot 5\\cdot a & ≡2\\cdot 5\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2\\cdot 3) \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{2}\\cdot 3) \\\\ 5a & ≡5b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $gcd(5,3)=1,$ by the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n5a≡5b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. By statement I and the first property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\\,⟺\\,5a≡5b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b17312d2-4961-5057-924d-78f6ff17fb06"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b17312d2-4961-5057-924d-78f6ff17fb06" :answer-field/id #uuid "b17312d2-4961-5057-924d-78f6ff17fb06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6072926a-de75-570c-be5c-7b19ca2fa4ed" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6072926a-de75-570c-be5c-7b19ca2fa4ed" "answer-165e395d-05d0-5648-8b98-661d9a74d37b" "answer-533aa886-6946-531f-bdb2-e7a060c00f71" "answer-5d847c60-18f9-5cd0-bc60-3e38b022ff75" "answer-76724f64-2846-5362-a726-6c451b64e577"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6072926a-de75-570c-be5c-7b19ca2fa4ed" :answer/id #uuid "6072926a-de75-570c-be5c-7b19ca2fa4ed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-165e395d-05d0-5648-8b98-661d9a74d37b" :answer/id #uuid "165e395d-05d0-5648-8b98-661d9a74d37b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-533aa886-6946-531f-bdb2-e7a060c00f71" :answer/id #uuid "533aa886-6946-531f-bdb2-e7a060c00f71" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d847c60-18f9-5cd0-bc60-3e38b022ff75" :answer/id #uuid "5d847c60-18f9-5cd0-bc60-3e38b022ff75" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76724f64-2846-5362-a726-6c451b64e577" :answer/id #uuid "76724f64-2846-5362-a726-6c451b64e577" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a253797f-7a56-5114-8318-23c6ded7e919" :question/id #uuid "a253797f-7a56-5114-8318-23c6ded7e919" :question/math-academy-id "q-213394" :question/problem "Given that $10a≡10b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)$\n- $9a≡9b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)$" :question/worked-solution "The division properties of modular arithmetic state the following:\n\n- For $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\n- For $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1,$ we have \n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Applying the first property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10a & ≡10b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,4) \\\\ 2\\cdot 5\\cdot a & ≡2\\cdot 5\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2\\cdot 2) \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{2}\\cdot 5) \\\\ 5a & ≡5b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $gcd(5,2)=1,$ by the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n5a≡5b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. By statement II and the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\\,⟺\\,9a≡9b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9f585a48-6faf-5a7b-8fa9-070db84aa8d5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9f585a48-6faf-5a7b-8fa9-070db84aa8d5" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f585a48-6faf-5a7b-8fa9-070db84aa8d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8e8650d8-740a-572c-9664-fc79147fe418" :answer-field/choices ["answer-abaca1a5-5cd1-5d44-ac31-4f1607333256" "answer-a657d1eb-66b3-50e4-a33a-a060eb891efe" "answer-8e8650d8-740a-572c-9664-fc79147fe418" "answer-09d37251-cd85-5560-a010-3e2285781892" "answer-0d7bfb9f-8cee-5d55-b979-3f79ae4ddbe2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abaca1a5-5cd1-5d44-ac31-4f1607333256" :answer/id #uuid "abaca1a5-5cd1-5d44-ac31-4f1607333256" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a657d1eb-66b3-50e4-a33a-a060eb891efe" :answer/id #uuid "a657d1eb-66b3-50e4-a33a-a060eb891efe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e8650d8-740a-572c-9664-fc79147fe418" :answer/id #uuid "8e8650d8-740a-572c-9664-fc79147fe418" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09d37251-cd85-5560-a010-3e2285781892" :answer/id #uuid "09d37251-cd85-5560-a010-3e2285781892" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d7bfb9f-8cee-5d55-b979-3f79ae4ddbe2" :answer/id #uuid "0d7bfb9f-8cee-5d55-b979-3f79ae4ddbe2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c54d6f9f-c7e1-5ec9-825f-3e37025371fc" :question/id #uuid "c54d6f9f-c7e1-5ec9-825f-3e37025371fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-213274" :question/problem "Given that $9a≡9b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,15),$ construct a statement that also must be true:" :question/worked-solution "The division property of modular arithmetic states that for $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have a common factor of $k=3,$ and the congruence can be written as\n\n$$\n3\\cdot 3a≡3\\cdot 3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3\\cdot 5).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can cancel out the common factor on both sides of the congruence and the modulus:\n\n$$\n\\cancel{3}\\cdot 3a≡\\cancel{3}\\cdot 3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{3}\\cdot 5)\\,⟺\\,3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-379863a3-9535-5888-911a-8a0b10fa2841" "answer-field-83f59b7b-ab84-5670-839c-3443e598aed3" "answer-field-74fe2f6b-5ac7-5a65-80ac-2d85b06d83d8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-379863a3-9535-5888-911a-8a0b10fa2841" :answer-field/id #uuid "379863a3-9535-5888-911a-8a0b10fa2841" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-f98cd691-8664-5ef9-bded-f1c52dfd5bff" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f98cd691-8664-5ef9-bded-f1c52dfd5bff" "answer-aaa4de33-cb4c-5b95-9a3b-3858732932e1" "answer-81b8fe68-f257-5f84-9fe7-fa0a9e9ae960"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f98cd691-8664-5ef9-bded-f1c52dfd5bff" :answer/id #uuid "f98cd691-8664-5ef9-bded-f1c52dfd5bff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:ans